      "anchor": "limits-continuity",
      "heading": "1. Limits & Continuity",
      "proseLatex": "Standard limits, indeterminate forms, L'Hospital's rule. A function is continuous at $a$ if $\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x) = f(a)$.",
      "keyFormulas": [
        {
          "formulaId": "M06-F01",
          "label": "Standard Limit",
          "latex": "$\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x} = 1$",
          "aiExplainContext": "Fundamental limit for trigonometric functions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "anchor": "derivatives",
      "heading": "2. Derivatives & Mean Value Theorems",
      "proseLatex": "Product/quotient/chain rules. Rolle's and Lagrange's MVT connect derivatives to function values.",
      "keyFormulas": [
        {
          "formulaId": "M06-F02",
          "label": "L'Hospital's Rule",
          "latex": "$\\lim f/g = \\lim f'/g'$ for 0/0 or $\\infty/\\infty$ forms",
          "aiExplainContext": "Evaluate indeterminate limits."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "workedExamples": [
    {
      "exampleId": "M06-EX01",
      "problemLatex": "If $f(x) = a|\\sin 2x| + b|e^{3x}| + c|2x - \\beta^2|$ is differentiable at $x=0$, find the condition.",
      "stepsLatex": [
        "$|\\sin 2x|$: not differentiable at 0 unless $a = 0$.",
        "$|e^{3x}| = e^{3x}$: differentiable everywhere.",
        "$|2x - \\beta^2|$: not differentiable at 0 unless $c = 0$."
      ],
      "answerLatex": "$2a + 3b = 0$"
    }
  ],
  "wbjeebTraps": [
    "Modulus functions are not differentiable at points where the argument is zero.",
